# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/)
# pages: the browser must check with the server on every visit (a quick "not modified" when nothing changed),
# so a new deploy shows up straight away and an old page is never served from the browser's cache
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# css, js and images: make-dist.sh stamps every link to them with ?v=<hash of the file> (stamp.py), so a changed
# file gets a new address and is fetched fresh; an unchanged one can be kept. "! Cache-Control" drops the rule above.
/css/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/js/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
